Well, the resulting battle with the four dragons was ...
anticlimactic.  You were right; not much to worry about at all, and I
am now disintegration resistant on top of everything else.  (Sleep
resistance came earlier on in the game in the form of some elf-
snacks.)

Actually, taken systematically, Fort Ludios did not offer much of a
challenge at all, except for perhaps eating all the trolls I killed
before they regenerated.  (No tinning kit.  No shops, actually, except
for one on level 3 and the ones in Minetown so far.  And I've delved
all the way to Medusa.)

So, here I am, basking in my victory, setting off landmines left and
right in the vault, tidying up almost 48,000 zm.  I find I'm way too
overloaded, so into the bag of holding they go.  Along with some
weapons, a couple of backup pieces of armor, about 150 rations, a few
scrolls, rings, potions and a couple of wands.

Including my newly identified wand of cancellation....

*headdesk many times*

All that effort, and I now have zero gold to my name, and a lot less
stuff.

I treated that wand, and my other unidentified wand, like dynamite
when I didn't know what they were.  I think my brain just registered
"Identified wand.  Must be good.  In it goes."

Heavy sigh....

Thankfully, most of that stuff was stuff was "Oh, this might be
useful...  into the bag it goes." stuff.  Most of the useful stuff I
stashed on Elbereth elsewhere in the fort.  I'm still kind of miffed
at losing some good wands and a few nice potions, though.  I just
don't know how I'm going to manoeuvre around in Medusa's lair.  I have
no way of crossing the water after spending a few thousand turns re-
scouring the dungeons for a pair of boots I haven't identified yet or
a ring or even a wand of cold.

At least I have another bag of holding....  Ah well, onward and
downard.

